## 0. Capture method

Describe how this discovery was produced. Future re-derivation depends on
using the same method (or a documented equivalent).

- **Tool:** `agent-browser network har start/stop` | Chrome DevTools HAR export | MITM | other
- **HAR location (offline only):** `/tmp/{{.Name}}.har` — **never inside the repo.** HAR files embed `Set-Cookie` headers and POST bodies; treat them as secrets.
- **Live session export:** `/tmp/{{.Name}}-cookies.json` (via `agent-browser cookies get --json`) — for cookie-jar auth (see §6.2).
- **Captured on:** _<date, store version, locale, account-state (guest/logged-in)>_.
- **Re-record trigger:** re-record when the platform ships a new backend version, when a fixture round-trip test breaks, or when an endpoint returns a shape different from the one pinned here.

### jq recipes used to filter the HAR

```sh
# All JSON API calls (method + status + URL)
jq -r '.log.entries[]
  | select(.response.content.mimeType | test("json"))
  | select(.request.url | test("google-analytics|segment|sentry|datadog|doubleclick|/collect|/track|/beacon|/log") | not)
  | "\(.request.method) \(.response.status) \(.request.url)"' /tmp/{{.Name}}.har

# Full detail for one endpoint
jq '.log.entries[] | select(.request.url | test("api/search"))
  | {request: {method: .request.method, headers: .request.headers,
     postData: .request.postData.text},
     response: .response.content.text}' /tmp/{{.Name}}.har
```

